ue was C$890M.\n- **For the guidance:** Backlog was C$5.1B at H1 2026, about 1.21× the guidance, and management says it covers 2027. H1 orders rose 11% year on year, led by utility and data-centre customers. Cancellations were under 1%.\n- **Against the guidance:**\n  - Industry transformer shipments fell 4% in Q2 2026, the first decline in three years.\n  - Voltaris's share of Caldrian transformer shipments fell from 31% to 27%.\n  - The Halbrook plant, its largest, was offline for nine weeks after a fire. It was already at full capacity when it restarted in August. Management's plan to recover the lost shipments by mid-2027 therefore needs it to run above normal capacity.\n  - The backlog may include orders that ship after 2027, and I couldn't check that.\n\nn2 reads Voltaris's own disclosures as supporting the guidance and put the odds slightly below even. n3 reads the industry data as pointing to C$3.5–3.8B. I weighted the two together because backlog and orders show demand, while the share loss and the capacity limit point to a delivery shortfall. Both nodes expect a miss of moderate size rather than a large one.\n\nSources: n2.r1 and n3.r1. The industry data covers only Q2 2026, and n3 had no 2027 market forecast.","ttft_ms":2096,"type":"result","duration_ms":32408,"uuid":"2b5fa8a8-aab9-491d-b964-7d776c8e3863","ttft_stream_ms":1538,"time_to_request_ms":436,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":31,"system_prompt":22,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":22,"input_attachments":94,"input_hooks":7,"conversation_append":0,"transcript_persist":49,"tool_pool_refresh":1,"init_message":46,"init_frame_send":14,"engine_pickup":1,"loop_entry":26,"message_prep":1,"model_config_wait":0,"autocompact":10,"request_announcements":38,"query_setup":3,"model_gates":0,"tool_schema_build":21,"message_normalization":2,"client_creation":19,"request_build":29},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_turn_index":0,"time_to_request_loop_lag_ms":199,"time_to_request_cpu_ms":72,"time_to_re